    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "A boy is twenty years younger than his father. In five years time the father will be three times the age of the boy. How old is the boy currently?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "5 years old.",
      "worked": "Let the boy's current age be $x$ years. His father's current age is $x+20$ years. In five years, their ages will be $x+5$ and $x+25$ years.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+25&=3(x+5)\\\\x+25&=3x+15\\\\25&=2x+15\\\\10&=2x\\\\x&=5\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe boy is currently 5 years old. In five years, he will be 10 and his father will be 30, which is three times his age.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
